# Build context exclusions.
#
# The builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is uploaded
# to the daemon and baked into that layer. Two reasons this matters:
#
#   1. Cache. Any change to an included file invalidates the COPY layer and
#      everything after it. Excluding .git means routine commits stop busting
#      the layer cache.
#   2. Correctness. The builder copies node_modules from the deps stage first,
#      then runs `COPY . .`. Without ignoring node_modules, a local build would
#      clobber the clean deps install with whatever is on the host.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies — supplied by the deps stage, never from the host
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — regenerated by `pnpm build`
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. These must never enter the build context. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# passed as build args instead (see Dockerfile ARG/ENV pairs in the builder).
.env
.env.*

# Editor / tooling
.vscode
.idea
.devcontainer
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Docs — not needed to build the app
README.md
*.md
LICENSE

# Scanner config, consumed by CI rather than the build
.trivyignore

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
